base=Path('.scratch/desktop-redesign')
findings=[
('HIGH','Typography','src/client/styles.css:281; src/client/workspace/workspace.css:48–72','Global footer padding adds 48px inside a fixed 240px card. The title flexes into the remaining space and clips through a line.','Scope page chrome styles; give card content a real layout budget. Auto-height by default, width resize, intentional line clamping with full details on selection.','Observed in the supplied screenshot and controlled Chromium. The full title can be reached in Cards/GitHub, but normal canvas reading repeatedly fails.'),
('HIGH','Layout / interaction','src/client/boards/IncomingWorkspace.tsx:163–182, 355','Add calls zoomToSelection with zero-duration animation, focuses the canvas and closes Incoming. Controlled add changed 100% to 237%.','Keep panel, scroll, search and focus stable. Add never changes zoom. Offer an explicit Reveal action for offscreen additions.','Every repeated add interrupts selection and spatial orientation; keyboard users also lose their place in the queue.'),
('MEDIUM','Layout','src/client/AuthLanding.tsx:131–149; src/client/boards/boards.css:1–28','Brand, nav, account, board title, Saved and settings stack above a bordered 70dvh canvas. Canvas starts around y=300 in the 1440×1000 audit.','Canvas fixed to the viewport edges. Two 40px floating control groups at 12px insets. No permanent header, page footer or sidebar.','Roughly 30% of initial viewport height is consumed before work begins. Opening repository connection adds still more document height.'),
('MEDIUM','Layout / navigation','src/client/AuthLanding.tsx:121–147; src/client/boards/Boards.tsx:56, 70; src/client/theme.ts:26','Plain internal href navigation and location.assign rebuild the document. Root opens the account landing page. Theme is applied after React mounts.','Persistent application shell with client navigation and history. Root restores the last board. Apply theme before first paint.','Document navigation is confirmed by source and browser flow. The user reports white flashes; exact first-paint flash timing was not instrumented.'),
('MEDIUM','Layout / workflow','src/client/boards/IncomingWorkspace.tsx:329–355; src/client/boards/incoming.css:6–12','Incoming starts with instructional paragraphs and repository-management controls. At 1440×1000 almost no candidate content is initially visible. No selection or batch action.','376px floating panel, compact search/filter area, 60–68px candidate rows, sticky selection footer. Move repository administration to Repositories.','The panel spends its space explaining itself rather than showing work. All rows need distinct title, identity, state and action zones.'),
('MEDIUM','Layout / workflow','src/client/RepositoryFinder.tsx:40–79; src/client/SourceBrowser.tsx:105–123; src/client/boards/IncomingWorkspace.tsx:286–344','Exact repository lookup requires submit. Existing title/kind filters apply only to loaded browser results; connection does not carry them into discovery. Loading subsequent pages is a manual command.','Immediate recent results, asynchronous typeahead over accessible repositories, direct URL resolution, prefilter preview, background paging and scroll prefetch.','The current flows expose transport steps and force users to repeat work. “Add all matching” must include unloaded matches, with honest completeness.'),
('MEDIUM','Layout','src/client/workspace/ItemCardShapeUtil.tsx:31–35','Cards have w:320/h:240 and canResize returns false.','Native width resize with a minimum width; content-aware height, optional expanded presentation and readable details at any zoom.','Users cannot fit real title lengths to their spatial arrangement. Width changes should reflow text rather than scale the type.'),
('MEDIUM','UI / layout','src/client/workspace/NativeWorkspace.tsx:57–63, 133–159; src/client/workspace/workspace.css:58–65','The drawing style palette, generic native toolbar, Cards disclosure and Incoming button compete as independent UI layers.','One compact board-control group; keep drawing tools compact at the bottom. Show drawing styles only for relevant tools/selections. Replace Cards with Find on board and contextual details.','Primary work controls lack a common placement, density and panel model. Preserve the keyboard list path in the replacement.'),
('MEDIUM','Writing','src/client/boards/IncomingWorkspace.tsx:333–347; src/client/SourceBrowser.tsx:73–77','“Receiving row”, “references”, “Discover next page” and “Reconcile source again” expose implementation mechanics.','Use “Incoming”, “Add selected”, “Checking for new items”, “Refresh”, and specific result counts. Explanations go into help or first-use hints.','Dense professional UI needs precise labels, not paragraphs compensating for surprising behavior.'),
('MEDIUM','UI / color','src/client/styles.css:52–68; src/client/workspace/workspace.css:1–25, 29–53; src/client/boards/incoming.css:2–6','The page, workspace and SDK each supply different control sizing, corners and surface treatment; workspace colors duplicate application tokens.','Shared semantic tokens and scoped component styles. 3px control/card corners, 4px floating panels, 1px structural lines, subtle overlay-only elevation.','The user explicitly requests a sharp modern direction. Radius alone is preference, not an accessibility defect; the inconsistency is systemic.')]
rows=''.join('<tr>'+''.join(f'<td>{escape(x)}</td>' for x in r)+'</tr>' for r in findings)
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>GitBored desktop audit and redesign proposal</title><style>
:root{font:15px/1.6 ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;color:#252c39;background:#f5f6f8}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0}main{max-width:1260px;margin:auto;padding:48px 36px 80px}h1{font-size:40px;line-height:1.12;letter-spacing:-.03em;max-width:800px;margin:14px 0 20px}h2{font-size:23px;line-height:1.3;margin-top:44px}h3{font-size:17px;margin-top:26px}p{max-width:86ch}a{color:#3449a1}small,.muted{color:#5c6676}.eyebrow{letter-spacing:.09em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:11px;font-weight:650;color:#596579}.lead{font-size:20px;line-height:1.5;max-width:850px}.actions{display:flex;gap:12px;margin:24px 0} .actions a{padding:9px 14px;border:1px solid #3449a1;text-decoration:none;border-radius:3px}.actions a:first-child{background:#3449a1;color:white}figure{margin:24px 0}img{width:100%;border:1px solid #d2d8e1}figcaption{font-size:12px;color:#5c6676;margin-top:7px}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;background:white}th,td{padding:12px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid #dce0e7}th{background:#e9edf2;font-size:11px}td:first-child{font-weight:650}.scroll{overflow:auto}.scroll table{min-width:1050px}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.box{background:white;border:1px solid #dce0e7;padding:20px}.box h3{margin:0 0 8px}li{margin:6px 0}code{font-size:12px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.verdict{border-left:3px solid #a52c3a;padding:12px 18px;background:#fff}.tiny{font-size:12px}@media(max-width:750px){main{padding:24px 16px}.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:32px}}
</style><main><div class="eyebrow">GitBored · Desktop only · 6 November 2026 · baseline 9266008</div><h1>The canvas is the application.</h1><p class="lead">Rebuild the experience around a full-viewport workspace, small floating controls and fast selection of GitHub work. Increase useful information density. Preserve spatial context.</p><div class="actions"><a href="proposal.html">Open interactive design study ↗</a><a href="#findings">Read the audit ↓</a></div><p>This proposal incorporates your direction: no separate landing page, no permanent sidebar, no tall header, sharp rather than pill-shaped surfaces, repository search as you type, preloaded results, automatic Incoming loading, prefilters, bulk add, resizable cards and no camera takeover.</p><figure><a href="proposal.html"><img src="evidence/proposal-light.png" alt="Proposed full-screen board with compact floating menus and a dense Incoming panel"></a><figcaption>Interactive visual study, using invented issue titles. Try filtering, selection, Add all matching, Undo, repository search, card details and the theme switch. This is an HTML interaction sketch, not a replacement canvas implementation.</figcaption></figure>
<h2>What went wrong</h2><p>The production composition lost the prototype’s organizing idea. Atlas put work on a full-page canvas and controls on top. Production put an editor into an account-oriented document page, then added feature controls independently. Generic page styles also leak into canvas content. Successful task tests established that actions work; they did not establish that using those actions repeatedly is efficient or pleasant.</p><p>Some complaints come from explicit earlier requirements: the spec requested a source section above the canvas, revealing each addition, and a prototype-derived tray close after Add. This proposal supersedes those interaction decisions. The native drawing engine, private board persistence, account isolation and separation of metadata from canvas history remain useful foundations.</p><figure><img src="evidence/original-atlas.webp" alt="Original Atlas contextual prototype with floating controls"><figcaption>The local Atlas reference: full canvas, composed controls, meaningful card hierarchy. The redesign keeps that structure while making controls sharper and Incoming more efficient.</figcaption></figure>
<h2>Scope and coverage</h2><p>Inspected the supplied desktop screenshot, original Atlas contextual screenshot/source reference, current React 19 + tldraw 5.6 composition, CSS tokens, navigation, boards, repository lookup/browsing, Incoming placement and card rendering. Read AGENTS.md, coding conventions, project management guide, issue-canvas spec and progress record. App source is unchanged.</p><table><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Evidence inspected</th><th>Result</th></tr><tr><td>Accessibility</td><td>Native buttons/labels, focus CSS, Incoming keyboard Add and Escape, Cards keyboard alternative; desktop enlarged-text capture.</td><td>Keyboard Add and Escape exercised; preserve the alternative list in redesign. Full screen-reader walk and automated accessibility scan not performed. No conformance claim.</td></tr><tr><td>Layout</td><td>AuthLanding, Boards, IncomingWorkspace, SourceBrowser; rendered desktop board and source panels.</td><td>Findings: shell, workflow, panel density, navigation and card sizing.</td></tr><tr><td>Writing</td><td>RepositoryFinder, SourceBrowser and IncomingWorkspace labels/status/recovery strings.</td><td>Implementation vocabulary and explanatory overhead. Existing explicit retry/reconnect recovery is useful and should remain near failures.</td></tr><tr><td>Typography</td><td>styles.css global footer; workspace card computed sizes; long fixture title and screenshot.</td><td>Confirmed title clipping and incorrect space allocation.</td></tr><tr><td>Colors</td><td>Application and workspace light/dark tokens; rendered theme screenshots; sampled declared foreground/surface contrast.</td><td>Token duplication. Sample text pairs pass; exhaustive rendered SDK/hover/selection contrast not verified.</td></tr><tr><td>UI polish</td><td>Styles for controls/cards/panels; native toolbar/style panel composition.</td><td>Mixed surface and density systems; redesign values below.</td></tr></table><p class="tiny">Mobile is deliberately excluded. Desktop width targets are 1280, 1440 and 1920px; current runtime captures cover 1280 and 1440. New layout at 1920 and actual browser 200% zoom are acceptance work. Enlarging root text to 200% is a separate check, not equivalent to browser zoom. Loading/error recovery was inspected in source; live GitHub failures and rate limits were not induced.</p>
<h2 id="findings">Ranked findings</h2><div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Severity</th><th>Domain</th><th>Location</th><th>Before</th><th>After</th><th>Why / evidence</th></tr>FINDINGS</table></div>
<h2>The proposed desktop workspace</h2><div class="grid"><div class="box"><h3>Small floating chrome</h3><p>Canvas fills 100% of the viewport. At top left: board switcher, compact save state and overflow menu. At top right: Find, Filters, Repositories, Refresh and Incoming count. No full-width header slab. Drawing tools float at the bottom; zoom is bottom left.</p><p>Identity, theme, sign out and board settings move into the left menu. Save failures produce a compact persistent actionable alert. A successful save never consumes a whole row.</p></div><div class="box"><h3>One panel model</h3><p>Small named controls open anchored non-modal panels over the canvas, without moving it. Use one utility panel at a time, with a stable screen position. Incoming stays open across adds, selection and canvas arrangement until explicitly closed.</p><p>Escape closes the active panel and restores trigger focus. Panel scrolling never scrolls the canvas. Card details flip/clamp to the visible viewport and switch directly between cards. No focus trap or backdrop.</p></div></div>
<h3>Density and visual language</h3><table><tr><th>Element</th><th>Proposed baseline</th><th>Purpose</th></tr><tr><td>Floating control bars</td><td>40px high; 12px from edges; 30–32px controls</td><td>Visible canvas between groups. 13px labels and 16px icons. Maintain at least 24px targets.</td></tr><tr><td>Panels</td><td>Incoming 376px; repository search 376–420px; details about 340px</td><td>Viewport-clamped height, header and actions fixed, body scrolls. No permanently reserved width.</td></tr><tr><td>Spacing</td><td>4 / 8 / 12 / 16 / 24px</td><td>4–8px within controls, 12px panel/card padding, stronger separation between groups.</td></tr><tr><td>Type</td><td>13px controls; 12–13px list content; 14px card titles; 11–12px metadata at 100% canvas zoom</td><td>Improve density by removing redundant content and padding first. Full details stay readable in screen coordinates at any canvas zoom.</td></tr><tr><td>Geometry</td><td>3px cards/controls; 4px overlays; 1px borders</td><td>Sharp rectangular surfaces. Subtle floating-panel shadows; no oversized radii, pills or decorative gradients.</td></tr><tr><td>Cards</td><td>About 260px wide and 176px tall with project fields</td><td>Repository and number together; title dominant; project Status / Weight / Priority / Sprint row; issue state, labels and assignee compact. Grow or deliberately clamp, never slice through a line.</td></tr></table><p>Counts and IDs use tabular figures. Use the existing system font and semantic theme tokens. Retain the prototype’s faint dot grid in both themes, with small consistent outline icons beside menu labels and for repository, issue/PR and status identity on cards. Icons supplement visible text. Keep primary emphasis to the commit action inside the active panel. Drawing styles appear only when relevant. Preserve any SDK attribution/licensing requirements rather than hiding them cosmetically.</p>
<h3>Product copy stays out of the way</h3><p><strong>Explicit user requirement:</strong> no explanatory subheaders, behavioral reassurance or implementation commentary in the final interface. Remove copy such as “Drag or add to the board. This panel stays open”, “Results are from repositories you can access”, “Preloaded” and “Positions retained”. Communicate through clear labels, familiar icons, grouping and behavior. Keep implementation and prototype explanations in this design document, not in product panels.</p><p>Retain concise information that helps someone act: result and selection counts, real loading progress, empty states with a next action, actionable errors and undo feedback. “Recently used” is a useful grouping; “preloaded” is an implementation detail. Avoid redundant subheaders under self-explanatory panel titles. Do not replace removed copy with tooltips that repeat the same commentary.</p><h3>Open the app → keep working</h3><p>Root restores the last accessible board and its view. The board switcher provides recent boards, search and New board. A first-time user sees an empty canvas with one compact “Connect GitHub” or “Connect a repository” panel. Authentication returns to that workspace. A deleted or unavailable last board opens the switcher over an empty canvas, with a clear recovery message. There is no marketing/account landing page in the signed-in flow.</p><p>Internal navigation stays in one application shell, supports browser Back/Forward and real link destinations, updates the title and moves focus appropriately. Board switching must flush or preserve pending edits before changing documents. Remember camera/view preferences per account and board outside document undo history. Apply the selected theme before first paint.</p>
<h3>Connect repositories without a page change</h3><ol><li>Open Repositories. Show connected and recently used repositories immediately from the current account’s authorized cache. Start refreshing the accessible repository index in the background.</li><li>Typing filters cached results immediately. After roughly 180ms, request additional authorized matches; cancel superseded requests and ignore stale responses. Support keyboard arrows/Enter, owner/name and pasted repository URLs.</li><li>Select a result to see a compact preview and import filters: state, issue/PR, labels and assignee. Default to Open, visibly editable. Show loaded counts honestly while more results arrive.</li><li>Connect in place. Discovery continues in the background; matching items populate Incoming. Keep connection filters attached to the source; let the user edit them later. Placement remains a separate explicit action.</li></ol><p>Preloading is bounded and account-scoped. Revalidate access before exposing private results; invalidate data on access loss/account changes. Fetch small pages and the next page ahead of scrolling, deduplicate by reference, reuse in-flight requests and back off on rate limits. Do not eagerly download every issue body. Server capability needs work: the current exact lookup and loaded-subset filters do not implement full authorized typeahead or persistent import queries.</p>
<h3>Incoming is a working list</h3><p>Its opening view shows work immediately: search, compact filter controls, then identifiable selectable rows. Each row shows title, number, type/state and one or two useful labels. A small plus adds one item; dragging places it precisely. Connection setup and source administration live in Repositories.</p><ul><li>Automatic next-page loading on scroll, plus bounded background prefetch. No “Discover more” or “Load page” button in the normal flow.</li><li>Search/filter applies to the intended source set, not just rendered rows. While incomplete, show a concise “Searching…” indicator beside the current match count. A partial result is never labelled complete.</li><li>Checkboxes, Shift range selection, Select matching, Add selected and Add all matching. Selection survives scrolling and background arrivals. A count identifies selections hidden by a changed filter; offer Clear selection.</li><li>Keep panel open, scroll position stable, query intact and keyboard focus at the next sensible row after Add. Announce the count without moving focus onto the canvas.</li><li>No-results state offers Clear filters. Initial loading uses compact row placeholders. Rate-limited or failed fetches keep already loaded items usable and show retry timing/action inline. Never interpret a failure as an empty repository.</li></ul>
<h3>Bulk add, placement and camera contract</h3><p><strong>Add all matching means all matching authorized results, including pages not yet loaded.</strong> Freeze the query when the user starts. Resolve remaining pages in bounded batches, show progress and Cancel, and make the eventual placement a single native undo operation. Cancel before commit leaves the board untouched. If retrieval fails, retain selection and show Retry; offer an explicitly labelled “Add the N loaded items” only as a separate choice. Respect current capacity limits (Incoming is capped at 20,000 references); report limits before partial placement.</p><p>Button additions go into a predictable staging area beside/below existing content, arranged in a compact grid. Existing objects retain exact coordinates and grouping. Newly added cards never force a zoom, pan or selection jump. An unobtrusive persistent result offers Reveal and Undo. Reveal pans minimally at the current zoom; Fit selection is an explicit separate command. Drag adds exactly where dropped. Deduplicate ordinary placement; preserve intentional native duplicates.</p><p>The visual study demonstrates fixed fixture results and reversible batch placement. It does not implement network paging, real tldraw history, cancelable remote discovery, native drag or persistence. Those are acceptance requirements, not claims about the mockup.</p>
<h3>Cards that behave like useful canvas objects</h3><p>Scope all card styles. Allow native width resize with text reflow, sensible minimum dimensions and content-aware height; avoid scaling the font to resize a card. Typical titles fit in two or three lines. Explicit compact presentation may clamp with an ellipsis; selection opens a full, readable title and details panel. Detail content uses screen-space type independent of canvas zoom. At distant zoom use a simplified representation instead of pretending tiny metadata is useful.</p><p>Preserve real links for opening GitHub, explicit hover/focus affordances and native selection/grouping/history. Find on board replaces the loose Cards disclosure with a searchable compact list and keyboard selection/reveal actions. It is also the accessible alternative to spatial navigation, not optional decoration.</p>
<h3>Related cards: Off · Selected · All</h3><p><strong>Added user requirement:</strong> make relationships between referenced GitHub issues and pull requests visible. The user explicitly prefers a useful, approximate “Related” connection over precise claims that a PR closes an issue. Do not require a dependency taxonomy or perfect closure semantics to deliver this view.</p><ul><li><strong>Selected (default):</strong> selecting a card reveals its connections and highlights adjacent cards. Clicking blank canvas clears the selection and lines. No hover-only activation or surprise camera movement.</li><li><strong>All:</strong> show thin, quiet connections between visible placed cards. Selected-card connections gain emphasis. Avoid making unrelated cards unreadable.</li><li><strong>Off:</strong> hide connectors. The per-card connection-count button explicitly shows that card’s neighborhood; card details retain a keyboard-accessible Related list.</li><li>Use a generic undirected line and “Related” label. Do not imply closing, blocking, dependency direction or guaranteed causality. Deduplicate repeated mentions between the same two items.</li><li>Only connect visible placements. A related item outside the board appears in the Related list with an explicit Add action; do not automatically populate the canvas. Filtered items remain filtered. For duplicate placements, prefer a single nearby visible counterpart rather than an all-to-all web.</li><li>Draw these as a view overlay behind the cards, recomputing anchors when cards move or resize. Keep user-drawn arrows independent. Store the mode per board/user, not in canvas undo history.</li></ul><p>The study demonstrates generic fixture relationships, mode switching, neighbor emphasis and direct related-card navigation. Production should normalize authorized provider links and cross-reference events into a deduplicated set of related item references. Cache and refresh with metadata; unavailable data is not a confirmed empty relation set. Do not fabricate connections from shared labels, titles or assignees, and do not expose inaccessible target identities.</p><p>GitHub exposes PR-linked issues through <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/graphql/reference/pulls">closingIssuesReferences</a> and mention relationships through <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/graphql/reference/issues">CrossReferencedEvent</a>. These are candidate retrieval sources, not a claim that integration already exists. The generic label also avoids falsely guaranteeing closure: <a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2025-04-23-users-can-now-choose-whether-merging-linked-pull-requests-automatically-closes-the-issue/">GitHub allows repositories to disable automatic issue closure</a>.</p>
<h3>Project fields on cards</h3><p><strong>Added user requirement:</strong> show project Status, Weight, Priority and Sprint directly on cards. Use one compact four-column row between title and footer; keep the title dominant and preserve the small issue/PR open/closed state as a separate attribute. The revised typical card is approximately 260 × 176px, putting previously empty space to work.</p><p>Choose a GitHub Project in board settings and map its field IDs to the four display roles. The sketch demonstrates Status → Status, Weight → Estimate, Priority → Priority and Sprint → Iteration. These are fixture mappings. Existing ticket 10 already covers planning-field mappings; extend it to explicitly include project status and priority. Do not infer a project status from issue open/closed state or assume weight, priority and sprint are universal issue fields.</p><p>An item in multiple projects uses the explicitly selected project; never silently combine values from different memberships. Details show project/field provenance and complete values. Confirmed empty values display “—”; numeric zero remains 0. Unavailable, unmapped, loading and not-in-project are distinct states in details, with concise indicators where needed on cards. Field retrieval remains authorized and separate from shape geometry/history. Refreshing values never moves cards. Card resizing and long-value handling must preserve readable labels, with full values in details.</p>
<h2>Implementation sequence</h2><ol><li><strong>Workspace shell and styling boundary.</strong> Full canvas, floating menus, no landing page, persistent internal navigation, first-paint theme, compact save/account states. Stop global styles affecting tldraw/card internals.</li><li><strong>Cards and spatial behavior.</strong> Readable title budget, native resizing, contextual details, Find on board, remove automatic add zoom/close. Preserve keyboard alternatives and native undo. Include project-field display/mappings and optional Related connections as explicit deliverables.</li><li><strong>Repository discovery and Incoming.</strong> One connection panel, authorized typeahead/cache, persistent import filters, automatic paging, selection and all-matching bulk operations.</li><li><strong>Integrated desktop acceptance.</strong> Real repositories and long titles; light/dark at 1280×800, 1440×900 and 1920×1080; keyboard and 200% zoom; loading/offline/rate-limit/access loss; persistence and batch undo.</li></ol><p>Use current React, CSS and tldraw. This is a redesign of the client composition and retrieval workflow, not a reason to replace the engine or storage. Review parked contextual-details work for reuse, but do not promote its unresolved clipping behavior. Update the prior source-host/auto-reveal requirements and tests that currently assert the tray closes. No tickets or production changes have been made by this audit.</p>
<h3>Acceptance criteria that protect the intended experience</h3><ul><li>Routine panels contain no explanatory subheaders or implementation commentary; labels, controls and behavior make their purpose clear.</li><li>Board canvas starts at viewport origin and fills it. Utility panels never change canvas bounds.</li><li>At 1440×900, Incoming exposes at least six typical rows plus filters and commit actions without explanatory setup blocks.</li><li>Add one or fifty: camera stays identical, old shapes stay identical, panel stays open, selection/filter context survives, one Undo restores the batch.</li><li>Connections switch between Off, Selected and All without moving cards; Related remains available by keyboard. Project fields use the chosen project and never conflate project status with issue state.</li><li>Titles have no partial-line clipping at default or resized dimensions. Full content is available by pointer and keyboard.</li><li>Typing a repository query immediately displays cached matches. Normal discovery and scrolling require zero manual pagination commands.</li><li>All matching is demonstrably complete across multiple pages, or visibly still resolving/limited. Partial failures do not claim success.</li><li>App entry and board switching retain the shell/theme, respect saves and restore the board view. No account landing page interrupts the task.</li></ul>
<h2>Verification and limits</h2><p>Safe audit runtime: <code>E2E_SOURCE_MODE=true E2E_APP_PORT=3015 E2E_PROVIDER_PORT=3016 E2E_FRONTEND_PORT=3009 CONTROLLED_SESSION_SECONDS=3600 pnpm exec tsx scripts/test-server.ts</code>. It used an isolated temporary database and the project’s controlled GitHub provider. The user’s app on 3001/3002 was left alone.</p><p><code>node .scratch/desktop-redesign/audit-runtime.mjs</code>: sign in → create board → connect fixture repository → load candidates → keyboard Add → reopen Incoming → add → dark theme → Sources → reopen board. Captures preserve the shell, connection panel, Incoming and 237% post-add zoom. Initial harness attempts exposed an allowlisted callback-port requirement and an early navigation into local draft recovery; these are audit-driver limitations, not product findings.</p><p><code>node .scratch/desktop-redesign/check-proposal.mjs</code>: checks fixture filtering, multi-select Add, persistent Incoming, Add all, Undo, repository typeahead, details, Escape and theme; captures 1440×1000 and 1280×800. See <a href="evidence/proposal-checks.json">check results</a> and <a href="evidence/runtime.json">runtime measurements</a>. No application build/gate was run: source was not changed.</p><p>Sample declared contrast pairs: application primary/secondary, card primary/secondary and accent links against their light/dark surfaces were computed with WCAG relative luminance; exact results are in <a href="evidence/contrast.json">contrast.json</a>. These samples do not certify the whole interface. Screen-reader behavior, complete error-state rendering, exact flash timing and live remote paging performance remain unverified.</p><div class="grid"><figure><img src="evidence/03-incoming.png" alt="Current Incoming panel devotes nearly all its visible space to instructions and source management"><figcaption>Current Incoming at 1440×1000.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="evidence/04-after-add.png" alt="Current add zooms to 237 percent and clips the title"><figcaption>Current Add: 237% zoom and a cut-through title.</figcaption></figure></div><p class="verdict"><strong>Verdict: Block.</strong> The confirmed card rendering and add/camera behavior materially harm the core workflow. The proposal is ready for design review; the production interface is not considered polished or accepted by this audit.</p></main></html>'''.replace('FINDINGS',rows)
# sibling prototype path from .scratch/desktop-redesign is three levels up
(base/'audit.html').write_text(html)
